    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/1/81089.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 25,
    "turn_text": "She actually had limited funds but had unlimited stamina. And she drew crowds from a lot of people, many of whom were unregistered, but came out in the sense of pride. I don't know whether anyone really thought Shirley Chisholm could win the primary to become president and certainly not to win in a national election. But the whole idea that she was speaking out for so many people who could not be heard and didn't have the courage to be out there, that there was just no question that Shirley Chisholm was a pioneer in the national level for African Americans and African American women.",
